{"id":"tour-divide","title":"Tour Divide (Great Divide Route)","who":"Classic bikepacking route; race since 2008","when":"Since 2008","vehicle":"Mountain or gravel bike","kind":"bike","color":"#15803d","media":[{"kind":"film","title":"Ride the Divide","note":"Documentary, 2010"}],"summary":"About 4,400 km of mostly gravel along the Rocky Mountains, from Banff in Canada to the Mexican border, crossing the Continental Divide again and again. The world's best-known bikepacking route: the fastest racers now finish in under twelve days; most riders take two months.","sources":[{"label":"bikepacking.com: Robin Gemperle wins the 2025 Tour Divide","url":"https://bikepacking.com/news/robin-gemperle-wins-the-2025-tour-divide/"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Tour Divide","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tour_Divide"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Great Divide Mountain Bike Route","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Divide_Mountain_Bike_Route"}],"approximate":"Towns on the route; the line between them follows roads, not the exact gravel tracks (use the official maps to ride it).","km":3808,"bbox":[-115.5722,31.333,-105.7648,51.1751],"stops":[{"name":"Banff","place":"Banff, Alberta","at":[51.1751,-115.5721],"text":"The start in the Canadian Rockies, in June, often with snow still on the passes."},{"name":"Elkford","place":"Elkford, British Columbia","at":[50.0245,-114.9218],"text":"Remote forest roads in grizzly country."},{"name":"Fernie","place":"Fernie, British Columbia","at":[49.5042,-115.0629],"text":"A mountain town before the US border."},{"name":"Eureka","place":"Eureka, Montana","at":[48.88,-115.0535],"text":"Into Montana at the Roosville crossing.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Eureka_Montana_Downtown_Looking_Northwest.jpg/500px-Eureka_Montana_Downtown_Looking_Northwest.jpg","page":"Eureka, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eureka_Montana_Downtown_Looking_Northwest.jpg","credit":"Royalbroil","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Whitefish","place":"Whitefish, Montana","at":[48.4108,-114.3346],"text":"Near Glacier National Park.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Downtown-whitefish-2006.jpg/500px-Downtown-whitefish-2006.jpg","page":"Whitefish, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Downtown-whitefish-2006.jpg","credit":"WikiCapa at English Wikipedia","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Seeley Lake","place":"Seeley Lake, Montana","at":[47.1553,-113.4484],"text":"Lakes and forest tracks south.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Seeley_Lake_Montana_20130716_04.JPG/500px-Seeley_Lake_Montana_20130716_04.JPG","page":"Seeley Lake, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seeley_Lake_Montana_20130716_04.JPG","credit":"Djembayz","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Helena","place":"Helena, Montana","at":[46.5927,-112.0363],"text":"Montana's capital, after big climbs.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Montana_State_Capitol_by_T._Elizabeth.jpg/500px-Montana_State_Capitol_by_T._Elizabeth.jpg","page":"Helena, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montana_State_Capitol_by_T._Elizabeth.jpg","credit":"Tracey Elizabeth","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Butte","place":"Butte, Montana","at":[46.0132,-112.5365],"text":"An old mining town on the Divide.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Butte_uptown.jpg/500px-Butte_uptown.jpg","page":"Butte, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Butte_uptown.jpg","credit":"WikiCapa (talk) (Uploads)","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Lima","place":"Lima, Montana","at":[44.6362,-112.5912],"text":"Wide, empty valleys towards Idaho.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Lima-Montana.jpg/500px-Lima-Montana.jpg","page":"Lima, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lima-Montana.jpg","credit":"Mark Hufstetler","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Island Park","place":"Island Park, Idaho","at":[44.4238,-111.3714],"text":"A short stretch through Idaho."},{"name":"Pinedale","place":"Pinedale, Wyoming","at":[42.8671,-109.861],"text":"Past the Tetons and the Wind River Range.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/PinedaleWyoming.jpg/500px-PinedaleWyoming.jpg","page":"Pinedale, Wyoming","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PinedaleWyoming.jpg","credit":"Tarabholmes","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Great Divide Basin","place":"Atlantic City, Wyoming","at":[42.4877,-108.7237],"text":"The Great Divide Basin: about 200 km with no water and no shade.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png/500px-NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png","page":"Great Divide Basin","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png","credit":"Pfly","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Rawlins","place":"Rawlins, Wyoming","at":[41.7908,-107.2392],"text":"Out of the basin.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/DowntownRawlins.jpg/500px-DowntownRawlins.jpg","page":"Rawlins, Wyoming","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DowntownRawlins.jpg","credit":"Vasiliymeshko","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Steamboat Springs","place":"Steamboat Springs, Colorado","at":[40.4848,-106.8317],"text":"Into Colorado's high country.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Steamboat_Springs_downtown.jpg/500px-Steamboat_Springs_downtown.jpg","page":"Steamboat Springs, Colorado","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Steamboat_Springs_downtown.jpg","credit":"katkimchee","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Breckenridge","place":"Breckenridge, Colorado","at":[39.4829,-106.0465],"text":"Boreas Pass at about 3,500 m, one of the highest points.","photo":{"url":"ht